start2park Park-and-Visit trips
-------------------------------

Dataset: trip_phases (the 96 trips that end in Frankfurt, November 2020 to
June 2021, as 223 stretches of driving, searching and walking)

Publisher: ReLUT, the Research Lab for Urban Transport at Frankfurt
University of Applied Sciences, from the start2park project.
https://github.com/ReLUT/parking-search-prediction/tree/main/Park-and-Visit

Licence: BSD 3-Clause License, as the repository's LICENSE states at the
pinned commit, reproduced in full at the end of this file.

Credit: start2park, ReLUT, Frankfurt University of Applied Sciences.
Copyright (c) 2023, ReLUT.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12 at 08:45:01 UTC from the publisher's
repository at commit de394ee98e37612da887b0e5cd9c87f8adf6a106:

  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ReLUT/parking-search-prediction/de394ee98e37612da887b0e5cd9c87f8adf6a106/Park-and-Visit/Dynamic_Park-and-visit_waypoints.csv
  (1,346,641 bytes, SHA-256 b50ff1b2faa3e158a2ed07835c0e3ef43d7f5127ed7e1faba44a7224d033fa04)
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ReLUT/parking-search-prediction/de394ee98e37612da887b0e5cd9c87f8adf6a106/Park-and-Visit/Dynamic_Park-and-visit_metadata.csv
  (16,944 bytes, SHA-256 8ad4e6f562855f51a442d1c934567eccd989f449437a11141e3ce73201eaff24)
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ReLUT/parking-search-prediction/de394ee98e37612da887b0e5cd9c87f8adf6a106/LICENSE
  (1,492 bytes, SHA-256 7b2c08c31495983a9451054a5e1710962ba9309b6fa67b427e52ab5fcb645716)

Kept: the trips whose last waypoint lies in Frankfurt (south of 52° N; the
study's Rostock trips are left out), whole, from where the driver set off
to where they walked to. Each trip is cut into stretches of one activity
(driving, searching, walking), each stretch running on to the first
waypoint of the next so the trip draws unbroken; a stretch of a single
waypoint at a trip's end draws nothing and is left out. From the metadata:
the search time, on-street or off-street, free, paid or illegal parking,
and whether the driver knew the destination. Times are as recorded, local
time. The waypoints' speeds are not kept.


Georeferenced street parking locations in Frankfurt am Main
-----------------------------------------------------------

Datasets: parking_spaces (29,215 parking spaces, one point each) and
parking_segments (5,518 street segments)

Publisher: Frankfurt University of Applied Sciences, on the Mobilithek,
offer 886571101635461120 ("Georeferenzierte Straßenparkstandorte in
Frankfurt am Main / Georeferenced street parking locations in Frankfurt am
Main"; temporal coverage 2024-01-01 to 2025-03-31).
https://mobilithek.info/offers/886571101635461120

Licence: Open Database License v1.0 (ODbL-1.0), the offer's standard
licence. The offer's condition for use: "This dataset contains information
from OpenStreetMap, which is made available here
(https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright) under the Open Database License
(ODbL)." The data was processed from OpenStreetMap with the OSM Parkraum
processing (https://github.com/osmberlin/osm-parking-processing, AGPL-3.0,
a licence of that code, not of the data).
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Credit: © OpenStreetMap contributors.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12 at 08:45:01 UTC from the offer's one
file (fetched with curl, which verifies the server's certificate):

  https://mobilithek.info/mdp-api/files/aux/886571101635461120/FFM_parking_data.zip
  (3,612,670 bytes, SHA-256 0420754ac53090a88d9385a8d401416d35848cc7885aed5fa7447ff0905ea8e2)
  of which parking_spaces_frankfurt.gpkg
  (21,643,264 bytes, SHA-256 972dafb3218234a72432558ea750af15b0f499f2feaa9d40a755e65e66f8f7bd)
  and parking_segments_frankfurt.gpkg
  (28,602,368 bytes, SHA-256 56044ef6d7bc2097290b0d448a01f66580a92b5fccf19af230cf2d6c1286c10b)

Kept: for each space, its street, side, orientation and position; for each
segment, its street, side, orientation, position, capacity and length, and
the spaces per 100 m worked out from them (zero where the supply marks no
parking, no figure where its data is missing or was not processed). The
template's datasets are a derivative database of the supply and stay under
the ODbL: anyone may use, share and adapt them, crediting
© OpenStreetMap contributors and sharing adaptations under the same
licence.


